    "What do all anagrams of a word have in common that other words do not?",
    "Sorting a word's letters gives the same key for every anagram (`\"eat\"`, `\"tea\"` and `\"ate\"` all become `\"aet\"`). Group words in a dictionary keyed by that, then sort as the statement asks.",
    "Grouping students by the first letter of their name uses the same dictionary-of-lists pattern, with a different key function."
